{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/types.ts#L467","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/types.ts:467"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Holds the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" option that every infinite query requires."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"extended-by","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extended by"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"InfiniteQueryPageParamsOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InfiniteQueryPageParamsOptions"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tpageparam","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TPageParam"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"property-initialpageparam\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialPageParam"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TPageParam"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The page param to start from when an infinite query has no pages yet. It is passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" for the first page; every page after that gets the value returned by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getNextPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPreviousPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":". It only applies while the query has no pages: once a first page exists, refetching starts from that page's own param instead."}]}]]}],"headings":[{"id":"extended-by","text":"Extended by","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tpageparam","text":"TPageParam","level":3},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/types.ts:467](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/types.ts#L467)\n\nHolds the `initialPageParam` option that every infinite query requires.\n\n## Extended by\n\n- [`InfiniteQueryPageParamsOptions`](InfiniteQueryPageParamsOptions.md)\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TPageParam\n\n`TPageParam` = `unknown`\n\n## Properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"property-initialpageparam\"></a> `initialPageParam` | `TPageParam` | The page param to start from when an infinite query has no pages yet. It is passed to `queryFn` as `pageParam` for the first page; every page after that gets the value returned by `getNextPageParam` or `getPreviousPageParam`. It only applies while the query has no pages: once a first page exists, refetching starts from that page's own param instead. |\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: InitialPageParam\ntitle: InitialPageParam\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/types.ts:467](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/types.ts#L467)\n\nHolds the `initialPageParam` option that every infinite query requires.\n\n## Extended by\n\n- [`InfiniteQueryPageParamsOptions`](InfiniteQueryPageParamsOptions.md)\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TPageParam\n\n`TPageParam` = `unknown`\n\n## Properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"property-initialpageparam\"></a> `initialPageParam` | `TPageParam` | The page param to start from when an infinite query has no pages yet. It is passed to `queryFn` as `pageParam` for the first page; every page after that gets the value returned by `getNextPageParam` or `getPreviousPageParam`. It only applies while the query has no pages: once a first page exists, refetching starts from that page's own param instead. |\n"}
